<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<sparql>
	<id><![CDATA[RetrieveBuildingElements]]></id>
	<!--
		Explanation:
		This SPARQL query returns the building elements
		of the model together with their geometry.
		1. In the graph <https://vng.nl/ontologies/ifc4add2> it matches the ontology classes ?ontType that are
		   ifcowl:IfcBuildingElement or any of its subclasses (rdfs:subClassOf*).
		2. Maps each ontology class IRI to the namespace used by the IFC instance data (?type) with:
		   BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(ifc:), STRAFTER(STR(?ontType), "#"))) AS ?type)
		   - STR(?ontType)    converts the class IRI to a string, for example
		                      "http://www.buildingsmart-tech.org/ifcOWL/IFC4_ADD2#IfcWindow".
		   - STRAFTER(..."#") keeps only the local name, for example "IfcWindow".
		   - STR(ifc:)        is the instance namespace
		                      "https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/DEV/IFC4/ADD2/OWL#".
		   - CONCAT(...)      joins the namespace and the local name.
		   - IRI(...)         turns the resulting string back into an IRI, for example
		                      <https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/DEV/IFC4/ADD2/OWL#IfcWindow>.
		   This is needed because the ontology graph uses the ifcowl: namespace,
		   while the IFC instance data uses the ifc: namespace.
		3. Finds the IFC elements (?ifcElement) whose rdf:type is one of those classes and that have an
		   ifc:globalId_IfcRoot, and reads the GlobalId string value (express:hasString).
		4. In the graph <https://vng.nl/geometries/> it matches the geometry with the same
		   geom:globalId and reads its geom:base64Data.
		5. Returns the distinct ?ifcElement, ?globalIdValue and ?base64Data, ordered by ?ifcElement.
	-->
	<query uri="retrieve-building-elements.ttl">
	</query>
</sparql>